+# Desktop meeting capture — TDD task list
+
+This is the DEV handoff for Forge issue `1ff834c9-d40a-4ff2-9095-b3ef9d11ff59`. Read [`plan.md`](./plan.md) first. Every task follows RED (new assertion demonstrably fails) -> GREEN (minimal passing implementation) -> REFACTOR (targeted suite remains green). Commit only after both Rust and web/package gates relevant to the task pass; never bypass Lefthook.
+
+## Stack and ownership rules
+
+- Rebase each PR on fresh `origin/main`, record the exact base SHA in the Forge issue, and re-prove the issue lease before edits.
+- Only this stack owns `apps/meeting-capture-desktop/**`, its root workspace/script entries, and its release workflow. Coordinate lockfile/root script edits; do not mix unrelated dependency upgrades.
+- The durability issue owns ingestion/ack/finalization prerequisites. The external connector owns `LocalCaptureSource`/evidence schemas. Terminal finalization owns the server finalizer. Caller-authority work owns candidates/tasks. If a missing prerequisite is found, stop and update Forge; do not duplicate it here.
+- Use physical Windows and macOS runners for native proofs. A mock-only result is incomplete.
+- Zero skipped/ignored/quarantined tests. A timeout, missing terminal summary, partial platform matrix, or unsigned artifact is not PASS.
+
+## PR 1 — Secure shell and native audio
+
+**Exact ownership**
+
+- New `apps/meeting-capture-desktop/package.json`, `src/**`, `tests/**`, `vite.config.*`, `vitest.config.*`
+- New `apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `build.rs`, `tauri.conf.json`, `capabilities/**`, `entitlements.plist`, `src/**`, `tests/**`
+- Root `package.json` workspace/test scripts and `bun.lock` only for this new package
+- New native test fixtures under `apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/tests/fixtures/**`; fixtures must be synthetic and redistributable
+
+### Task 1.1 — Scaffold the least-privilege collector shell
+
+RED: add tests that fail unless the capability manifest exposes only enumerated recorder/auth/update commands; CSP rejects remote scripts/navigation; frontend input cannot select a filesystem path, URL, shell command, or secret; calendar suggestions cannot invoke `start_capture`.
+
+GREEN: add the smallest Tauri 2 package and local UI with signed-out/permission/ready states, typed IPC wrappers, immutable Product-Suite origin configuration, no shell/filesystem/process/global-HTTP plugins, and exact locked dependencies.
+
+Commands:
+
+```powershell
+bun run --cwd apps/meeting-capture-desktop test -- --run tests/security-boundary.test.ts tests/start-authority.test.ts
+cargo test --manifest-path apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml security_boundary -- --exact
+bun run --cwd apps/meeting-capture-desktop lint
+bun run --cwd apps/meeting-capture-desktop typecheck
+```
+
+### Task 1.2 — Make consent and permission preflight executable
+
+RED: platform-adapter tests cover missing/denied/revoked mic or system permission, hidden-window start, permission changes after ready, device disappearance, no signal, and close-window during recording. UI tests require separate mic/system status and meters plus a persistent tray/window indicator.
+
+GREEN: implement explicit preflight and a Rust-owned capture state transition. Only a foreground click token may start; permission errors are actionable; closing requires stop confirmation; no auto-start entry point exists.
+
+Commands:
+
+```powershell
+bun run --cwd apps/meeting-capture-desktop test -- --run tests/permissions.test.ts tests/recording-indicator.test.ts
+cargo test --manifest-path apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml permissions
+```
+
+### Task 1.3 — Prove Windows native WASAPI plus mic capture
+
+RED: Rust contract tests fail for non-monotonic frames, missing `source_kind`, duplicate intervals, endpoint changes, device loss, silence, pause/resume overlap, and COM cleanup. The Windows physical harness first records failing evidence before an implementation is enabled.
+
+GREEN: implement a Windows-only `SystemAudioSource` with the `windows` crate using shared-mode WASAPI loopback, event-driven capture, monotonic timestamps, and clean endpoint reinitialization; implement mic input behind the same typed frame contract without mixing sources.
+
+Commands on supported Windows x86_64:
+
+```powershell
+cargo test --manifest-path apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml --target x86_64-pc-windows-msvc audio::contract
+cargo test --manifest-path apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml --target x86_64-pc-windows-msvc wasapi
+bun run --cwd apps/meeting-capture-desktop test:native:windows
+```
+
+Physical evidence: headphones and speakers, default endpoint switch, unplug/replug, mic denied/revoked, sleep/wake, silence, 60-minute capture, and resulting gap/timestamp report. Store only synthetic-source hashes and metrics, never captured speech.
+
+### Task 1.4 — Prove Core Audio Process Tap plus mic capture
+
+RED: macOS adapter/contract tests cover pre-14.2 rejection, missing usage description, first-run denial, revocation, aggregate-device failure, target/process exit, output-device change, sleep/wake, silence, and teardown. Start the physical spike with a failing proof record.
+
+GREEN: implement a macOS 14.2+ Core Audio Process Tap adapter with the minimum entitlement/usage description, monotonic frames, device recovery, and separate mic frames. No ScreenCaptureKit dependency or screen permission is allowed.
+
+Commands on macOS Intel and Apple Silicon:
+
+```bash
+cargo test --manifest-path apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml audio::contract
+cargo test --manifest-path apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml core_audio_tap
+bun run --cwd apps/meeting-capture-desktop test:native:macos
+```
+
+Blocking physical evidence: first-run/deny/grant/revoke, active process and whole-system target where supported, process exit, output switch, Bluetooth reconnect, sleep/wake, silence, mic simultaneous capture, and 60-minute Intel/Apple-Silicon runs. If either architecture fails the contract or performance gate, stop PR 1 and return to PLAN for ScreenCaptureKit evaluation.
+
+### PR 1 gate
+
+Run:
+
+```powershell
+bun run --cwd apps/meeting-capture-desktop lint
+bun run --cwd apps/meeting-capture-desktop typecheck
+bun run --cwd apps/meeting-capture-desktop test -- --run
+bun run --cwd apps/meeting-capture-desktop build
+cargo fmt --manifest-path apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml --check
+cargo clippy --manifest-path apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings
+cargo test --manifest-path apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml --all-features
+cargo audit --file apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.lock
+```
+
+Require both physical platform reports, all security-boundary tests, and the idle/recording CPU-memory/bundle budgets. PR 1 may merge without backend upload but must not present itself as a usable production recorder.
+
+**PR 1 rollback:** revert the PR; it has no server or persisted-user-data dependency. Remove only test app credentials/capabilities created for the spike.
+
+## PR 2 — Encrypted spool, acknowledgements, and recovery
+
+**Entry gate:** PR 1 is landed. Local durability `d88d461a-c259-4dc6-a751-f2b3c6898b7a` and the external connector `LocalCaptureSource` contract are landed on `origin/main`; record exact SHAs and generated contract version in Forge.
+
+**Exact ownership**
+
+- `apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/src/spool/**`, `crypto/**`, `credential_store/**`, `upload/**`, and their Rust tests
+- `apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src/api/**`, recovery/status UI, and package tests
+- `packages/sdk/src/**` plus matching tests only if the landed durable API lacks a generated/typed desktop client; do not change the server endpoint or contracts in this PR
+- Existing `LocalCaptureSource` adapter fixtures only to add the desktop source conformance case, with its owner’s review
+
+### Task 2.1 — Encode the contract and fail-closed authenticated client
+
+RED: contract tests reject wrong actor/tenant, missing/expired auth, arbitrary base URL, malformed session, missing consent, unsupported topology, same sequence/different digest, acknowledgement mismatch, unexpected redirect, and any response that tries to grant candidate/task authority.
+
+GREEN: use the landed Product-Suite create/upload/status/delete contracts through a typed client. Store opaque credentials only in Keychain/DPAPI, bind sessions to the server actor, and project the landed `LocalCaptureSource` evidence fields without local interpretation.
+
+Commands:
+
+```powershell
+cargo test --manifest-path apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml auth_client
+cargo test --manifest-path apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml upload_contract
+bun run test:contracts
+bun run test:sdk
+```
+
+### Task 2.2 — Persist ciphertext before upload
+
+RED: deterministic filesystem-fault tests fail for crash before/after flush/rename, reused nonce, plaintext discovery, manifest downgrade, path traversal/symlink, altered ciphertext/AAD, missing key, wrong ACL, full disk, quota edge, concurrent writers, and chunk marked eligible before durability.
+
+GREEN: implement per-session AEAD keys in OS secure storage, encrypted versioned manifests/chunks, unique nonces, owner-only ACLs, atomic same-directory writes, flush ordering, and the 2-GiB/eight-hour quota. Never use SQLite or another data service.
+
+Commands:
+
+```powershell
+cargo test --manifest-path apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml spool::faults
+cargo test --manifest-path apps/meeting-capture-desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml spool::confidentiality
+bun run --cwd apps/meeting-capture-desktop test -- --run tests/spool-status.test.ts
+```
+
+### Task 2.3 — Implement idempotent upload, acknowledgement, and backpressure
+
+RED: virtual-clock/fake-server tests cover offline start, disconnect during body/response, lost ack, duplicate replay, out-of-order ack, 401/403, 409 digest conflict, 413, 429 with `Retry-After`, 5xx, timeout, TLS/hostname failure, app restart, and queue saturation. Assert upload concurrency never exceeds two and no ciphertext is deleted without a matching durable ack.
+
+GREEN: upload only durable chunks, use bounded exponential backoff with full jitter, honor server rate limits, reconcile status after ambiguous responses, and delete after exact session/sequence/digest acknowledgement. Capture pauses visibly before quota/data loss.
+
+Commands:
+
